<!--
  Slide 12 — Per-Engineer View
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from metrics.json):
    {{ENG_LABELS}}     Mermaid xychart-beta x-axis array string. Shape:
                       a JSON array literal of double-quoted strings,
                       e.g., '["<engineer-1>", "<engineer-2>", ...,
                       "<engineer-N>", "Blitzy Agent"]'. Sourced from
                       metrics.json:"per_engineer.labels". The Blitzy
                       Agent row appears at the end of the array per AAP
                       §0.8.1 (Engineering Actor Framing).
    {{ENG_VALUES}}     Mermaid xychart-beta bar-values array string.
                       Shape: a JSON array literal of integers or
                       decimals, e.g., '[<v1>, <v2>, ..., <vN>,
                       <vBlitzy>]'. Sourced from
                       metrics.json:"per_engineer.values". Positional
                       correspondence to {{ENG_LABELS}} is required:
                       the Nth element of values pairs with the Nth
                       element of labels.
    {{METRIC_LABEL}}   Metric display label, e.g., "<metric-name>
                       (Metric <N>)". Sourced from
                       metrics.json:"per_engineer.metric_label". The
                       per-engineer breakdown is defined for metrics 2,
                       4, 5, 6, 10 per AAP §0.8.5.
  Required non-text visual: <pre class="mermaid"> xychart-beta

  Authority: AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory), §0.7.1 Rule 4 (Mermaid title + legend
  required), §0.7.1 Rule 5 (content-slide constraints), §0.8.1 (Engineering
  Actor Framing — Blitzy Agent is one row in the after period), §0.8.5
  (Per-Engineer Views — real names for metrics 2, 4, 5, 6, 10).

  Rendering notes:
    - xychart-beta is a Mermaid 11+ feature; the deck pins Mermaid 11.15.0
      via CDN per AAP §0.6.1, so this syntax is guaranteed to render.
    - Inside <pre class="mermaid">, "xychart-beta" must be at column 0;
      inner declarations are indented by four spaces. Whitespace is preserved.
    - {{ENG_LABELS}} and {{ENG_VALUES}} are substituted as raw JSON arrays
      (including surrounding [ and ]), which is also the literal x-axis and
      bar array syntax of Mermaid xychart-beta.
    - The renderer is the single source of truth (metrics.json); the engineer
      ordering and bar values here must match the Per-Engineer Acceleration
      table in acceleration-report.md (Rule 4 — Internal Consistency).
-->
<section class="content-slide eng-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Per-Engineer View</span>
  <h3>Contributions by Engineer · After Period</h3>
  <pre class="mermaid">
%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"xyChart":{"backgroundColor":"#FFFFFF","titleColor":"#1A105F","xAxisLabelColor":"#1A105F","xAxisTitleColor":"#1A105F","xAxisTickColor":"#1A105F","xAxisLineColor":"#1A105F","yAxisLabelColor":"#1A105F","yAxisTitleColor":"#1A105F","yAxisTickColor":"#1A105F","yAxisLineColor":"#1A105F","plotColorPalette":"#5B39F3,#94FAD5,#2D1C77,#1A105F"}}}}%%
xychart-beta
    title "{{METRIC_LABEL}}"
    x-axis {{ENG_LABELS}}
    y-axis "Contribution"
    bar {{ENG_VALUES}}
  </pre>
  <table class="eng-name-table" aria-label="Engineer name reference">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Chart label</th><th>Full name</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
{{ENG_TABLE_ROWS}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="diagram-legend"><i data-lucide="info" aria-hidden="true"></i> Chart x-axis uses short labels for readability; the table maps each short label to the engineer's full display name (per AAP §0.8.1, Blitzy Agent appears as one row in the after period; real names use resolved aliases in actor_aliases.json).</p>
</section>
